## Mission description

Under the hierarchical supervision of the Deputy Head of the Education, Higher Education and Research Unit France (Paris), with a close functional link to the Project Secretariat (Rome). The Coordinator of the Expertise France component – MED CAMPUSES – corresponds to the focal point of Expertise France within the Project Secretariat and vis-à-vis the Steering Committee.

Based mainly at the Expertise France office in Rabat, with regular missions to countries of intervention (Tunisia, Morocco, Jordan, Egypt, Lebanon, and Libya) and participation in project governance bodies (Rome/Brussels).

The Coordinator oversees the entire MED CAMPUS component, the centerpiece of the project South anchorage. They represent Expertise France within a tripartite consortium comprising MAECI-Italy FIAP-Spain, and EF-France, operating under the “Team Europe” framework. The ability to work effectively within a consortium and maintain strong institutional relationships—with the European Commission as donor; Italian partners (MAECI/EUTALIA/Uni-Italia); Spanish partners (FIAP); and key stakeholders, including the Secretariat of the Union for the Mediterranean (UfM) and UNIMED—is critical to the project’s success.

The position requires a **confirmed project management profile**, with proven expertise in s**etting up and monitoring grants** (sub-granting mechanisms towards MED Campus, leveraged grants at Téthys), in **multi-budget management country**, and a real **diplomatic and partnership capacity** to navigate between donor, implementing partners and higher education institutions. Knowledge of the academic sector is an asset but not the heart of the position: it is above all an operational, financial, and institutional steering post.

**Key responsibilities**

*Strategic management and governance*

- Oversee and manage the entire programmatic cycle of the 8 MED Campus (selection, needs assessment, development of action plans, deployment of technical assistance and grants);
- Ensure programmatic consistency across the 8 MED Campuses and alignment with the strategic directions approved by the Steering Committee and the Secretariat;
- Oversee the operationalisation of the Intra-MENA Mobility Scheme within the Expertise France component;
- Lead, in collaboration with Téthys, the programmatic and financial dimension of the crosscutting gender equality and inclusion project.

*Team management and coordination*

- Supervise the Grant Officer and ensure the functional coordination of the Higher Education expert and experts mobilised in the short term on the component;
- Work in close coordination with the Project Support Unit (PSU) and with the headquarters in Paris.

*Institutional and partnership relations*

- Represent Expertise France within the Secretariat and before the Steering Committee; maintain relations with the Directorate-General for the Middle East, North Africa and the Gulf (DG MENA) of the European Commission (donor);
- Ensure institutional coordination with the Italian unit (MAECI) and FIAP on the Spanish side, and develop partnership relations in a "Team Europe" consortium approach;
- To be the privileged interlocutor of Expertise France with the French institutions involved in the project — the Téthys network (Aix-Marseille University), Campus France, and the MESR — and ensure that their respective contributions are properly coordinated with the implementation of the MED Campus;
- Maintain regular dialogue with UfM, UNIMED and other academic partner networks.

*Administrative, financial and grant management*

- Manage and arbitrate the EF component budget, oversee administrative, financial and procurement procedures (in liaison with the USP team in Rabat);
- Supervise the grant mechanism at MED CAMPUS and the grant to Téthys (setup, contracting, financial monitoring, compliance) in conjunction with the Grant Officer;

*Reporting and accountability*

- Ensure all the narrative and financial reporting for the component, in coordination with the Secretariat and the other Team Europe units, including the preparation of the inception report and the semi-annual reports;
- Ensure internal reporting at Expertise France (progress reports, alerts, monitoring indicators) in collaboration with headquarters.

## Project or context description

The **Mediterranean University** project is a Euro-Mediterranean initiative jointly led by three entities: the Italian Ministry of Foreign Affairs (MAECI) as lead consortium, FIAP for Spain, Expertise France for France, in indirect management of the European Commission. The project is **36 months, with a budget of €12.2 M in total (including €2.6 M for EF including €100,000 in co-financing from the MEAE),** covering all countries in the Mediterranean basin, including **10 Southern Neighbourhood partner countries.**

This initiative aims to sustainably strengthen cooperation in the fields of higher education, research and innovation between the European Union and partner countries on the southern shore of the Mediterranean. It is part of the Pact for the Mediterranean, which makes education and youth priorities for rapprochement between the two shores.

The action is based on the establishment of the Secretariat of the "Mediterranean University", in charge of coordinating two complementary pillars:

- **University Consortiums:** already mature alliances (North-South) quickly delivering joint degrees, mobility, and mutual recognition—piloted on the Italian.
- **The MED Campus:** hosted by universities on the southern shore, organized around 8 thematic priorities linked to the Pact for the Mediterranean, aiming to build these universities' institutional capacity so that they eventually become consortium leaders ("seeds" of the next generation of consortia).

**Expertise France’s** role is specifically concerned with the overall coordination of the MED Campus component as described below.

- Operational and administrative management of support provided to the 8 thematic MED Campus, methodological consistency between them and with the program’s strategic directions;
- Grants linked to the action plans of each campus;
- Support for the operationalization of an Intra-Mena Mobility Scheme;
- Technical assistance on request to selected institutions;
- Strategic articulation with key partners: **Tethys** (university network coordinated by Aix-Marseille Université, 100+ universities/22 countries), the **MESR, among others;**
- Steering, with Téthys, the cross-cutting gender equality and inclusion project

This is a first phase that will notably allow for the establishment of common governance, launch two university consortia and up to eight MED Campuses, and lay the foundations for a larger-scale deployment of the initiative. A second phase could be expected after these three years.

## Required profile

- Higher education (Bac+5) in international project management, international relations, political science or equivalent;
- Proven experience (8-10 years) in managing EU-funded international cooperation projects, ideally in indirect management;
- Solid expertise in grant management and sub-granting mechanisms, multi-country budget management;
- Excellent capacity for negotiation and management of multi-stakeholder partnership relations (donors, ministries, counterpart agencies);
- Experience working in an international consortium and a multicultural environment;
- Knowledge of the higher education sector is desired but not essential;
- Current imperative English (working language of the project); French and/or Arabic are assets;
- Availability for regular trips in the region.

Créée en 1922, DanChurchAid (DCA) est une organisation non gouvernementale Danoise dont l’action est basée sur les droits. Installée en RCA depuis 2015, DCA fournit une assistance aux communautés les plus démunies en situation de conflit et de post-conflit au travers de son Programme d’Action Humanitaire: éducation aux risques des Armes Légères et Petit Calibres (ALPC), des Restes et Explosifs de Guerre (REG) ; Réduction de la Violence Armée (RVA) et consolidation de la paix & Support Psycho social , distribution des semences et outils, appui aux organisations de la Société Civile pour leur implication dans la réforme du Secteur de Sécurité (RSS).

DCA recherche **Un(e) Assistant(e) Logistique** trèsexpérimentés pour participer au développement et la mise en œuvre des activités.

**OBJECTIF DU POSTE :**

Sous la supervision du Prolog Manager, l’assistant Logistique aide le responsable de la logistique à assurer un fonctionnement efficace des systèmes et services liés à la gestion des stocks et l’ensemble des activités en lien avec les flux des items.

Il organise le support logistique aux programmes dans le respect des procédures DCA.

Il assiste le responsable de base ou le coordinateur logistique dans la mise en œuvre des règles de sécurité.

**RÔLES ET RESPONSABILITÉS :**

- **Approvisionnement (Achat) :**
- Aider à mener des études de marché lorsque cela est nécessaire et communiquer des informations sur les tendances du marché ;
- Aider à s'assurer que tous les achats sont effectués à temps et mis à jour sur le système en ligne de DCA (ADMIND) ;
- Assister le Chargé logistique approvisionnement et le Prolog dans la gestion de l'archivage ;
- Aider au suivi des rapports logistiques mensuels du pays ;
- Aider à tenir à jour le suivi des achats.

**Gestion des Stocks**

- Aider à organiser les différentes réceptions de stock des articles conformément au bon de commande/Contrats ;
- Faire des mises à jour dans le logiciel Admind avec un suivi minutieux ;
- Préparer et organiser les différentes expéditions entre les différents bureaux de DCA en RCA ;
- Aider l’assistant logistique en charge des stocks dans les différentes tâches ;
- Aider à créer et actualiser les différentes fiches de stock ;
- Documenter tous les IN-OUT du stock dans le logiciel Admind ;
- Aider l’assistant logistique des stocks dans les inventaires et reporter dans le logiciel Admind.

**Gestion Flotte (Fleet)**

- Aider le logisticien base dans la supervision des opérations de maintenance et de réparation ;
- Assurer la gestion des carnets de bord et son remplissage ;
- Aider le logisticien base dans la formation des chauffeurs ;
- Assurer la gestion des documents administratifs de chaque moyen roulant ;
- Faire le suivi de consommation du carburant avec des analyses ;
- Faire la mise à jour des informations dans Admind.

**Gestion des locaux**

- Sous la supervision du logisticien base, inventorier les biens de DCA dans toutes les Guest-houses ;
- S’assurer des différentes réparations dans les locaux de DCA avec les normes en place ;
- Assurer le suivi des différents paiements des baux et autres coûts annexes.

**Gestion des Assets (Equipements)**

- Réceptionner et codifier tous les équipements en fonction des bailleurs si nécessaire avec l’appui du chargé logistique base ;
- Faire la mise à jour des informations dans le logiciel Admind ;
- Renseigner tous les IN-OUT des Assets dans Admind.

**Compétences techniques en suivi et évaluation**

- Pour réussir dans ce poste, les candidats doivent faire preuve des compétences suivantes :
- Organisation : Un excellent sens de l'organisation pour gérer efficacement les responsabilités liées à ce poste ;
- Interpersonnelles : Des compétences relationnelles solides, avec une capacité à établir des relations professionnelles positives et à travailler en équipe.
- Compétences Informatiques : Bonne maîtrise de MS Office (Word, Excel, Outlook) est exigée.
- Attention aux Détails : Une grande attention aux détails pour garantir l'exactitude et la qualité du travail.
- Diplôme de niveau Bac+2/+3 en logistique.
- Minimum de 3 ans d'expérience dans la logistique sur un poste similaire, idéalement au sein d'une ONGI.

**Le poste est réservé uniquement aux candidats de la nationalité centrafricaine.**

Créée en 1922, DanChurchAid (DCA) est une organisation non gouvernementale Danoise dont l’action est basée sur les droits. Installée en RCA depuis 2015, DCA fournit une assistance aux communautés les plus démunies en situation de conflit et de post-conflit au travers de son Programme d’Action Humanitaire: éducation aux risques des Armes Légères et Petit Calibres (ALPC), des Restes et Explosifs de Guerre (REG) ; Réduction de la Violence Armée (RVA) et consolidation de la paix & Support Psycho social , distribution des semences et outils, appui aux organisations de la Société Civile pour leur implication dans la réforme du Secteur de Sécurité (RSS).

DCA recherche **Un(e) Assistant(e) IT** trèsexpérimentés pour participer au développement et la mise en œuvre des activités.

**OBJECTIF DU POSTE :**

Sous la supervision du Responsable IT ou de toute autre personne désignée par la Direction, l’Assistant IT assure le support informatique quotidien du personnel et contribue au bon fonctionnement, à la sécurité et à la disponibilité des équipements et systèmes informatiques de l’organisation.

Il/Elle participe à l’installation, à la configuration, à la maintenance et au suivi des équipements informatiques, des logiciels, des réseaux et des outils de communication, afin de garantir la continuité des activités du bureau et des équipes sur le terrain.

**RÔLES ET RESPONSABILITÉS :**

**Assistance et support informatique**

- Fournir une assistance technique de premier niveau aux utilisateurs pour résoudre les problèmes liés aux ordinateurs, imprimantes, logiciels et autres équipements informatiques ;
- Diagnostiquer les pannes matérielles et logicielles et assurer leur résolution dans les meilleurs délais ;
- Assister le personnel dans l’utilisation des outils informatiques et des applications professionnelles ;
- Installer, configurer et mettre à jour les systèmes d’exploitation, les logiciels et les applications autorisées ;
- Assurer le suivi des demandes d’assistance et tenir un registre des incidents informatiques.

**Gestion et maintenance du matériel informatique**

- Participer à l’installation, à la configuration et à la maintenance préventive des ordinateurs, imprimantes, scanners et autres équipements informatiques ;
- Assurer le suivi du parc informatique et tenir à jour l’inventaire des équipements ;
- Préparer les équipements informatiques destinés aux nouveaux employés et récupérer ceux des employés en fin de contrat ou en mobilité ;
- Signaler les équipements défectueux et proposer des solutions de réparation ou de remplacement ;
- Veiller à la bonne utilisation et à la conservation des équipements informatiques de l’organisation.

**Gestion des réseaux et de la connectivité**

- Assister dans la configuration et le suivi des réseaux locaux (LAN), du Wi-Fi et des connexions Internet ;
- Identifier et signaler les problèmes de connectivité et contribuer à leur résolution ;
- Participer au suivi des équipements réseau, des routeurs, des points d’accès et des autres dispositifs de communication ;
- Assurer, sous supervision, le suivi des prestataires chargés de la maintenance informatique et des services Internet.

**Sécurité informatique et protection des données**

- Veiller au respect des procédures de sécurité informatique de l’organisation ;
- Participer à l’installation et à la mise à jour des antivirus et autres outils de protection autorisés ;
- Sensibiliser les utilisateurs aux bonnes pratiques en matière de sécurité informatique, notamment la gestion des mots de passe et la prévention des courriels frauduleux ;
- Contribuer à la sauvegarde régulière des données conformément aux procédures internes ;
- Signaler immédiatement tout incident de sécurité, perte de données ou accès non autorisé au Responsable IT ;
- Respecter strictement la confidentialité des informations et des données auxquelles il/elle a accès.

**Gestion des comptes et des outils numériques**

- Participer à la création, à la configuration et à la désactivation des comptes utilisateurs, sur autorisation du responsable compétent ;
- Assister le personnel dans l’utilisation des outils de messagerie électronique, de visioconférence et de collaboration ;
- Contribuer à la gestion des droits d’accès aux ressources informatiques selon les autorisations établies ;
- Apporter un appui technique lors des réunions, formations et autres activités nécessitant des équipements informatiques.

**Gestion administrative et reporting**

- Tenir à jour les registres de maintenance, les fiches d’inventaire et les rapports d’incidents informatiques ;
- Préparer des rapports périodiques sur l’état du parc informatique et les difficultés rencontrées ;
- Participer à l’élaboration des besoins en équipements, accessoires et consommables informatiques ;
- Contribuer au suivi des mouvements de matériel et à la documentation des interventions techniques ;
- Exécuter toute autre tâche pertinente relevant de ses compétences, à la demande de son supérieur hiérarchique.

**Qualifications et compétences requises**

**Formation**

- Être titulaire d’un diplôme de niveau Bac+2 ou Bac+3 en informatique, systèmes et réseaux, maintenance informatique ou dans un domaine équivalent ;
- Toute formation complémentaire en cybersécurité, administration réseau ou assistance informatique constitue un atout.

**Expérience professionnelle**

- Justifier d’au moins deux (2) années d’expérience dans un poste similaire, idéalement au sein d’une ONG, d’une entreprise ou d’une organisation disposant de plusieurs bureaux ;
- Une expérience dans l’assistance aux utilisateurs et la maintenance d’un parc informatique est souhaitable.

**Compétences techniques**

- Bonne maîtrise des systèmes d’exploitation Windows et des outils bureautiques ;
- Connaissances pratiques en installation et maintenance des ordinateurs et imprimantes ;
- Connaissances de base en réseaux informatiques, Wi-Fi et connectivité Internet ;
- Maîtrise des outils de messagerie et de collaboration professionnelle, notamment Microsoft 365 ou des solutions équivalentes ;
- Connaissances de base en sauvegarde, antivirus et sécurité informatique ;
- Capacité à diagnostiquer les problèmes techniques et à documenter les interventions.

Créée en 1922, DanChurchAid (DCA) est une organisation non gouvernementale Danoise dont l’action est basée sur les droits. Installée en RCA depuis 2015, DCA fournit une assistance aux communautés les plus démunies en situation de conflit et de post-conflit au travers de son Programme d’Action Humanitaire: éducation aux risques des Armes Légères et Petit Calibres (ALPC), des Restes et Explosifs de Guerre (REG) ; consolidation de la paix & Support Psycho social , Activités Génératrices de Revenu (AGR); distribution des biens non alimentaires et ménagers (NFI), , distribution des semences et outils, appui aux organisations de la Société Civile pour leur implication dans la réforme du Secteur de Sécurité (RSS).

DCA recherche **01 Officier Logistique** expérimentés pour la mise en œuvre de ses activités.

**OBJECTIFS DU POSTE**

Le/Le/la Chargé(e) Logistique est chargé (e) de la gestion logistique et de la supervision du charroi automobile, du matériel roulants et équipements durables (tous équipements avec espérance de plus de 2 ans) au niveau de sa Base.

Sous la supervision du Chef de Base en lien fonctionnel avec le Prolog Manager, Il organise le support logistique au niveau de sa Base dans le respect des procédures DCA.

Il assiste le Chef de Base en lien avec le Prolog Manager dans l’accomplissement des taches dévouée au département de la logistique de sa base.

**Gestion du charroi automobile, matériel Roulants et équipements durables**

Sous la supervision du Chef de Base en lien avec le Prolog Manager, participer à la négociation des contrats de location du matériel roulants et équipements durables ;

- Superviser la planification et l’exécution des opérations de maintenance et de réparation du matériel roulants et des équipements durables. ;
- Etablir le planning des mouvements du matériel roulant et des équipements durables ;
- S’assurer de la composition et de la présence du carnet de bord et son remplissage au quotidien pour tous les matériels roulants et équipements durables ;
- Garantir de façon permanente la formation générale des chauffeurs et des logisticiens terrains et procéder à un contrôle régulier de leurs renforcements de capacité ;
- S’assurer que l'équipe des chauffeurs et logisticiens terrains respectent les procédures et les règles lés à la gestion du charroi propres à DCA ;
- Vérifier la présence, la mise à jour et la bonne utilisation des carnets de bord ;
- Faire le suivi, l’analyse, la consolidation et le compte-rendu du niveau de consommations de carburant et des index kilométriques pour chacun des roulants au sein de sa Base ;
- S’assurer de la présence, du classement et du suivi des documents administratifs pour chacun du matériel roulant.

**Gestion de l’approvisionnement**

- Sous la supervision du Chef de Base en lien avec le Prolog Manager, garantir le suivi et le respect des lignes budgétaires affectées à la logistique en lien avec la gestion et supervision du matériel roulants et des biens ;
- Organiser les dossiers d’achats des biens et services et appuyer le Prolog dans la rédaction des contrats et bons de commande ;
- Garantir la mise en œuvre des achats en veillant au respect des règles et procédures de validation ;
- Participer à l’Identifier des items à acheter dans les différents bureaux et ceci en lien avec le matériel roulant et les biens ;
- S’assurer que les dossiers d’achats sont complets et archivés dans ADMIN selon les procédures DCA.

**Gestion du parc**

- Mettre à jour en temps réel l’inventaire du charroi automobile et des biens et assurer le suivi du matériel ;
- **Optimiser la répartition du matériel selon les besoins des activités**

**Gestion des stocks**

- Mettre en place un plan de suivi des stocks des biens de l’organisation dans les différents bureaux de DCA et s’assurer de la sécurisation des espaces d’entreposage ;
- S’assurer des bonnes conditions de stockage du matériel et veiller à l’application des systèmes FIFO et FEFO ;
- S’assurer du respect des procédures pour les entrées et sorties de stock ;
- Garantir la bonne tenue de la documentation liée au stockage ;
- Superviser l’inventaire physique mensuel des stocks.

**Autres**

**Reporting / Capitalisation**

- Assurer le suivi DA et informer les demandeurs de l’avancement du traitement de leurs commandes ;
- Consolider mensuellement le pack logistique et le faire remonter au coordinateur logistique :
- Suivi des achats ;
- Suivi des stocks ;
- Suivi des véhicules ;
- Suivi conso ;
- Suivi des Thuraya ;
- Suivi des équipements ;
- Faire remonter les dossiers achat des programmes clôturés à la coordination selon la périodicité établie.

**Compétences et connaissances requises :**

Pour réussir à ce poste, vous devrez avoir un bon sens de l’organisation. Des compétences relationnelles et de discrétion sont indispensables. De bonnes connaissances dans le domaine de la logistique et bonne ma$itrise des outils bureautiques et informatiques.

Niveau Bac+3 en en logistique, vous disposez de 3 ans d'expérience au moins à un poste similaire. Avoir un bon style de communication, faire preuve de dynamisme et de rigueur, avoir un esprit de travail d'équipe.

**Le poste est réservé uniquement aux candidats de la nationalité centrafricaine.**

## **COOPI is looking for a Head of Mission (National Candidates Only) in Somalia**

COOPI has been active with its humanitarian and resilience programs in Somalia since 1984.

**COOPI has been implementing emergency and long-term resilience-building projects, including food security & livelihoods, water and sanitation and health, to improve the living conditions of thousands of vulnerable families.**

COOPI has been providing response and supporting the most basic and pressing needs of communities in Southwest State, South Central, Banadir, Jubaland and Somaliland. COOPI has a long-standing presence in those locations, providing both emergency humanitarian support and building resilient livelihoods through a multi-sectoral approach with a specific focus on crisis-affected populations. COOPI's main operational and coordination offices are located in Mogadishu, Baidoa and Dollow. COOPI also has a support and regional office in Nairobi.

**COOPI is currently implementing projects funded by Australia DFAT, ECHO, AICS.**

In Kenya, COOPI has been present since 1992 and has managed interventions in rural development; access to water, food security, cash assistance, shelter and healthcare.

## **Purpose of the role**

**The Head of Mission is responsible for the management and coordination of the foreign offices (Somalia and Kenya) in different aspects: guarantees the correct implementation of the projects in both countries, mission development, budget sustainability, security, staff management and positioning within relevant clusters and working groups.** Collaborates with the Regional Coordination or directly with headquarters in the definition of the country strategy and intervention priorities.

### **Main responsibilities**

**RAPRESENTATION**

- **Manages relations with the main institutional donors and with potential ones**;
- Represents COOPI in the country/area by engaging in relations with institutions, NGOs, local and international organisations and partners;
- S/He is responsible for the image of the organisation in the country;

**DEVELOPMENT**

- Verifies and proposes to the Regional Office the intervention priorities to consolidate COOPI's positioning in the country;
- Contributes to the definition of the Country Strategy and the country planning (projects and coordination).

**MANAGEMENT**

**Project's management**

- Coordinates and directly monitors projects, guaranteeing the correct implementation in conformity with the contractual obligations and donors’ procedures, and in line with COOPI’s procedures and management standards;
- S/he is responsible for the coordination of the proposal drafting process and the documents’ preparation aimed at the submission of new projects;
- **S/he is responsible for the good quality of project reports and the preparation of monitoring documentation required by headquarters;**
- Ensures the transmission of all official and administrative project documentation to headquarters;

**Foreign office management**

- **S/he is responsible for all different aspects related to the country office management**: economic and financial situation, local regulations, office organization charts, logistics, local and expatriate personnel management, in conformity with the organization’s guidelines;
- Guarantees the respect of the country’s legislation and administrative regulations;
- Has power of attorney for legal signature on documents and accounts;

**Staff management**

- S/he is responsible for the local staff management, in compliance with the law of the country;
- Participates and supports in the selection of the expatriate staff;

**Security Management**

- **S/he is responsible for staff security,** for the correct implementation and respect of the general security rules;

**Economic and financial management**

- **S/he is responsible for the country’s economic results;**
- Supervises the financial management and ensures that all financial reporting deadlines and donor/COOPI’s procedures are respected;
- Participates in the projects/coordination budget preparation;

**Visibility**

- Cooperates with the Communication and Fundraising office for all communication, awareness and fundraising activities implemented in and for the country.

### **Requirements**

**ESSENTIAL**

- University degree in relevant subjects;
- **Minimum 5 years of relevant working experience in international relief and development, of which minimum 3 years in the role;**
- Excellent oral and written communication and negotiation skills, multitasking and organizational skills;
- **Experience in liaising with governmental/local authorities, IOs and NGOs;**
- Demonstrated ability to work in stressful environments and under pressure;
- Proven capacity in managing a team;
- Fluency in the **English language**;
- Computer literacy.

**DESIRED**

- Experience in working in conflict-prone environments;
- Experience in logistics, procurement and security matters;
- Previous work experience in Somalia and Kenya;
- Experience in managing complex consortium/partnerships.

We reserve the right to close the vacancy prior to the application closing date, once a sufficient number of applications has been received. **Please note that only the shortlisted candidates will be contacted.**

*COOPI Cooperazione Internazionale is an Italian secular and independent humanitarian organisation fighting against all forms of poverty to improve the world. Founded in 1965, today COOPI is present in 27 countries in Africa, Latin America and the Caribbean and the Middle East, with both emergency and development projects carried out by expatriate staff – an average of over 200 people per year – and national staff. The main institutional funders are the European Union – ECHO and INTPA – USAID, UN agencies, the Italian Government, local authorities and other European Governments.*

Tiered Approach

In line with the commitment to safeguard capacity and support personnel already in the Organization, a majority of UNDP UNCDF/UNV vacancies are advertised using a tiered application process whereby:

- Tier 0 : UNDP/UNCDF/UNV IP staff holding permanent (PA) and fixed-term (FTA) appointments, whose posts will be abolished, or contracts will be terminated or not renewed during 2026.

- Tier 1 : Other UNDP/UNCDF/UNV staff holding permanent (PA) and fixed-term (FTA) appointments

- Tier 2 : UNDP/UNCDF/UNV staff holding temporary appointments (TA), personnel on regular PSA contracts, and Expert and Specialist UN Volunteers

- Tier 3 or no tier indicated : All other contract types from UNDP/UNCDF/UNV and other agencies, and other external candidates

Please make note of the Tier(s) indicated in the vacancy title, if any, and ensure that you satisfy the eligibility to apply.

Background

In order to address the challenges and adapt to the continually evolving scenario in the Bangsamoro Autonomous Region in Muslim Mindanao (BARMM), continuing substantive support for governance, stabilization, resilience and normalization processes will be crucial to help address risks and vulnerabilities and protect and sustain the gains of the Bangsamoro peace process. The DFAT-Australia support through UNDP-implemented programs has significantly contributed to conflict-prevention and peacebuilding in the Bangsamoro. Phase 1 of PROSPER-Bangsamoro has sought to complement and strengthen the conflict-prevention and peacebuilding ecosystem in the BARMM through support across governance, stabilization and resilience, and normalization outcomes. Given the current fragile context emerging from evolving risks and challenges to the peace process, there is an imperative to further strengthen this conflict-prevention and peacebuilding ecosystem in the lead-up to the first Bangsamoro Parliamentary Elections in September 2026. The gains secured from DFAT-Australia support will need to be further consolidated and deepened amidst fractures in the peace process.

Phase 2 of PROSPER-Bangsamoro will thus seek to build on the gains and lessons learned from the implementation of the initial phase. It will continue to contribute to all three outcomes of Peacebuilding in Conflict-Affected Mindanao (PCAM) 2 – governance, stability and normalization by continuing good practices while enhancing implementation approaches based on challenges encountered in the initial phase. Moreover, Phase 2 of PROSPER Bangsamoro will continue to strengthen the capacities of BARMM and local government institutions for meaningful, inclusive and peace governance through responding to perceptions of exclusion and grievances among communities and groups in marginalized and vulnerable situations. It will continue to contribute to efforts on conflict prevention and transformation not only at the level of peace process mechanisms and government institutions, but also bridging and deepening social transformation to effectively address the needs, rights and aspirations of communities and sectoral groups who lie at the heart of the Bangsamoro peace process. As the transition to the regular Bangsamoro Government follows the September 2026 elections, Phase 2 will also assist partners in consolidating, transitioning and institutionalizing conflict-sensitive and peacebuilding policies, capacities and programs at the regional, LGU and national levels.

Phase 2-PROSPER-Bangsamoro aims to achieve the following outcomes:

- Outcome 1: Effective transition of conflict-sensitive and peace-responsive governance policy and programming facilitated at the regional and local government;

- Outcome 2: Empowerment and resilience of sectoral groups and their capacities for rights-claiming processes strengthened in the transition to the regular Bangsamoro Government; and,

- Outcome 3: Normalization processes supported through transitional justice and reconciliation programming, delivery of peace dividends and accompaniment support for GPH-MILF peace process mechanisms.

In implementing PROSPER-Bangsamoro Phase 2, the Project will partner with Bangsamoro regional and local government institutions as well as civil society organizations and local social formations representing groups in marginalized and vulnerable situations in the region, such as women, youth, Indigenous Peoples and former combatants. The Project will also actively coordinate with national government agencies and peace mechanisms in the design and implementation of some components of PROSPER-Bangsamoro Phase 2.

Building on the networks established and strengthened under the previous conflict-prevention and peacebuilding programmes supported by Australian Embassy and implemented by UNDP Philippines, Phase 2-PROSPER Bangsamoro will work with women peacebuilders and mediators, youth advocates, Indigenous Peoples representatives, and members of Moro liberation fronts.

To support the Peacebuilding Cluster under the Peace and Stabilization Team, and primarily to assist in the implementation of Phase 2-PROSPER-Bangsamoro, UNDP is seeking an Finance and Administrative Officer based in Cotabato City. This position will support the Project in the day-to-day financial management, monitoring, reporting and operational coordination of PROSPER-Bangsamoro, and may also provide finance and administrative support to other peacebuilding projects under the Cluster, as required.

The Finance and Administrative Officer is tasked to assist in the administration, review and monitoring of financial transactions of the Project, and thus ensuring high quality, accurate and consistent finance and administrative support for the Project. S/he is expected to report on a daily basis to the Project Manager. The position holder also demonstrates a client-oriented approach, tact and ability to work with people of different national and cultural backgrounds. Moreover, the Finance and Administrative Officer works in close collaboration with the UNDP Peace & Stabilization Programme Team, the Cotabato Field Office Team as well as with other UN Agencies, government officials, technical advisors and experts, multilateral and bi-lateral donors and civil society organizations to successfully implement Peacebuilding projects.

Duties and Responsibilities

Under the overall guidance of the Team Leader of the Peace and Stabilization Programme Team, and the Head of Cotabato Field Office and under the direct supervision of the Peacebuilding Project Manager, the Finance and Administrative Officer is responsible for providing effective financial and administrative support primarily to PROSPER-Bangsamoro and, as required, to other projects and initiatives under the Peacebuilding Cluster of the Peace and Stabilization Programme Team.

S/he analyzes, interprets and reports according to UNDP Financial Rules and Regulations, as guided by the UNDP Programme and Operations Policies and Procedures (POPP). The Finance and Administrative Officer helps to promote a collaborative, client-oriented approach consistent with UNDP rules and regulations.

The Finance and Administrative Officer will be directly responsible for successfully completing the below set of tasks within allotted, agreed-upon time frames:

Ensures the implementation of financial management strategies and adapts processes and procedures focusing on achievement of the following results:

- Full compliance with UNDP rules, regulations, policies and strategies, financial recording/ reporting system and implementation of effective internal controls, proper functioning of a customer-oriented financial resources management system;

- Continuously review the financial situation and support the project in the preparation of forecasts and periodic disbursement requests to be submitted to the donor;

- Supports the development of funding requests, negotiations and amendments to the contribution agreement;

- Review and approve the funding authorization and expenditure certificate (FACE) from partners as and when required;

- Facilitate annual audits; and

- Regularly monitor financial exception reports for unusual activities and transactions and review anomalies or unusual transactions and inform the supervisor of the results of the review and the corrective actions being proposed;

- Ensure that all financial transactions, reports, and supporting documentation are compliant with the requirements of the Contribution Agreement and UNDP’s Policies and Procedures;

- Conduct quality assurance checks prior to the submission of financial reports to the donor, ensuring accuracy, completeness, and adherence to the donor’s reporting formats and standards;

- Lead the preparation, formatting, and consolidation of donor financial reports, ensuring that all financial data is properly organized, verified, and supported with compliant documentation prior to submission;

- Prepare payment requests and ensure the timely processing of disbursements in line with UNDP’s POPP and donor requirements;

- Coordinate with relevant UNDP units, implementing partners, and project teams to gather financial data and inputs required for budget preparation, expenditure monitoring, and donor reporting;

- Work in close collaboration with the UNDP Country Office Finance Analyst, ensuring operational-level financial implementation aligns with the Country Office’s strategic financial oversight and quality assurance functions;

- Finalization of the financial sections of the update of the progress report and the disbursement request and preparation of quarterly and biannual forecasts of cash flows and annual cash flows;

- Timely review and finalization of the improved financial report and other ad hoc financial reports as required by the project;

- Timely preparation of program budget reviews and provision of justifications for budget reallocation / reprogramming requests;

- Preparation and monitoring of budgets; regular analysis and reporting on budget approvals and delivery status;

- Monitor and ensure that donor contributions are properly transferred to UNDP in a timely manner;

- Ensure that advance payments and direct payments are properly reviewed and made in a timely manner, and ensure that payment information is correctly recorded in the Quantum system in a timely manner;

- Ensures proper management of cash receipts and petty cash; and

- Maintenance of the proper filing system for finance records and documents.

Ensures implementation of project operations focusing on achievement of the following results:

- Provide effective financial support to the implementation of Peacebuilding projects;

- Ensure timely and quality financial support to project activities;

- Facilitate the conduct of personnel performance appraisal; monitor personnel leave credits and absences;

- Undertake any additional tasks as assigned by the Project Manager.

Ensures proper project cash management functioning focusing on achievement of the following results:

- Timely review of resource balance to ensure availability of sufficient funds for implementation and appropriate disbursements;

- Timely identification and registration of receipts for the income request;

- Timely preparation of monthly cash flow forecasts for use by supervisor.

Provides technical advice and support for effective and efficient financial control in the project, focusing on achievement of the following results:

- Analyze and interpret the financial rules and regulations of UNDP, and assist in providing solutions to issues related to finance, logistics and day-to-day office administrative activities, while, promoting a collaborative, client-focused, quality and results-oriented service;

- Provision support for planning of financial resources of the Peacebuilding Cluster projects, such as preparation of reports containing analysis of the financial situation; preparation, planning, monitoring and revisions of budgets; regular analysis and reporting on the budget approvals and the delivery situation;

- Maintenance of the internal expenditures control system, including budget checks and timely corrective actions on unposted vouchers, the vouchers with budget check errors, match exceptions, and unapproved vouchers;

- Process documents for cash advance, liquidation, reimbursements in a timely manner, for submission to and approval of the Project Manager, Head of Cotabato Field Office and UNDP Peace and Stabilization Team Leader;

- Preparation of non-PO vouchers for the project and payrolls for salaries and other benefits due to project staff;

- Certify expenditures for approval of payments and monitor/control budget expenditures and approved allotments; and,

- Coordinate and act as focal point for issues relating to finance.

Ensures facilitation of knowledge building and knowledge sharing focusing on achievement of the following results:

- Organization/conduct of training for the projects staff on financial management;

- Synthesis of lessons learnt and best practices in finance and administration;

- Capacity building of implementing partners on overall financial management;

- Sound contributions to knowledge networks and communities of practice; and,

- Provide accurate, prompt and appropriate information and reports to the Project Manager on financial matters of the project.

Ensures quality assurance of overall office management and financial arrangements:

- Perform office management as well as management of procurement systems, policies and procedures in accordance with UNDP guidelines;

- Oversight and quality assurance of administrative, logistics, procurement, and asset management functions undertaken by the Administrative and Logistics Assistant;

- Contribute to the timely and accurate liquidations of cash advances and review of related documents;

- Support ensuring that requests for travels are in accordance with UNDP guidelines;

- Quality assurance and oversight of monthly payment orders (MPOs), claims for reimbursement of travel expenses and other entitlements, and receipt of goods and services and provisioning are properly carried out in accordance with IPSAS and UNDP policies and procedures;

- Timely corrective actions on unrecorded vouchers, including vouchers with budget verification errors, match exceptions, unapproved vouchers;

- Timely response to requests from headquarters to resolve financial data issues.

The incumbent performs other duties within their functional profile as deemed necessary for the efficient functioning of the Office and the Organization.

